@startuml review_correlated_02_field
' Review unit 02 of 04 -- see docs/review_correlated.md for the series.
' State AFTER commit df6419f (src +354, tests +117).
' Every number below is from a run of the cases at commit df6419f.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/review_correlated_02_field.puml

title Unit 02 -- CorrelatedField: a smooth Gaussian field, not yet wired (7eb2025..df6419f)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #777777
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  DiamondBorderColor #777777
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #8899AA
  FontColor #33495E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #C8C08A
}

start

partition "GenerateData: unchanged" {
  :case S, case A: byte-identical to unit 00, serial equals parallel
  data_structure still raises TypeError: nothing calls the new class yet;
}

partition "CorrelatedField(seed, var_idx, num_dims, varying_dims, correlation_length, noise)  (NEW)" {
  #C8E6C9:resolve_lengths(correlation_length, num_dims): one entry per dim
  None -> 10 sites on every dim; a number -> that length on every dim
  a list -> one entry per dim: >= 1 sites, 0 (white), None (constant)
  0 < L < 1, negative, NaN, inf, non-number, wrong length -> ValueError;
  #C8E6C9:rng = stream(seed, <b>Stream.CORRELATED_FIELD</b> (NEW tag 12), var_idx)
  draws, always all of them and in this order:
    phases   uniform(0, 2 pi), 64
    gaussian standard normal, 64 x num_dims
    white    uniform(-pi, pi), 64 x num_dims;
  #C8E6C9:wavenumbers k[m, d], for each varying dim d:
    L >= 1 -> gaussian / L     L == 0 -> white     L None -> 0
  constant (pinned) dims of the variable: 0;
}

#FFF9C4:example: CorrelatedField(77, var 0, 3 dims, varying [0, 1, 2], default)
lengths 10, 10, 10; std of k per dim 0.1005, 0.0939, 0.1014 (target 1/L = 0.1);

partition "apply(uniform, global_indices)  (NEW)" {
  #C8E6C9:blocks of 16384 occupied sites -> _sum_waves(block):
  for each of the 64 waves, site by site:
    angle = phi[m] + sum_d k[m, d] * i_d        (float64, dims in fixed order)
    angle -= 2 pi * rint(angle / 2 pi)          (into [-pi, pi])
    total += cos(float32(angle))
  S = total * sqrt(2 / 64);
  note right
    No matrix product or 2-D reduction:
    a site's value then comes from the
    same operations whatever the array
    length, so a chunk reproduces the
    serial run bit for bit. float32 cos
    is ~7x faster; values move < 1e-7.
  end note
  #C8E6C9:noise > 0: z = sqrt(1 - noise^2) * S + noise * ndtri(clip(u))
  u' = ndtr(z): uniform over (0, 1) again   (scipy, NEW dependency);
}

#FFF9C4:the example field on every site of [4, 8, 8], row x0 = 0, x1 = 0:
x2 = 0..7:  0.392 0.436 0.487 0.540 0.590 0.632 0.663 0.681
correlation of neighbours along x2: <b>0.994</b> (unit 00 values: 0.167)
evaluated in two parts (split after a third of the sites): bit-identical;

partition "CorrelatedField.per_variable(...)  (NEW, used from unit 03)" {
  #C8E6C9:data_structure, noise: spread_per_variable (unit 01)
  unknown data_structure -> ValueError
  correlation_length or noise with no correlated variable -> ValueError
  one noise value: applied to the correlated variables only
  a noise list with a value > 0 on an uncorrelated variable -> ValueError
  length longer than its axis, on a dim a correlated variable
  varies along -> UserWarning ("default correlation_length ..." if not given)
  returns one CorrelatedField per correlated variable, None otherwise;
}

stop

legend right
  |<#C8E6C9> green |= added or changed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFCDD2> red |= removed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFE0B2> orange |= single-variable flow touched by THIS unit |
  |<#FFF9C4> yellow |= generated data or file that changed as a result |
  | plain | unchanged since unit 01 |

  <b>What to review in unit 02</b>
  * the draw order (it is part of the data)
  * k per dim: Gaussian, white, constant
  * _sum_waves: per site, fixed order, float32 cos
  * noise through ndtri / ndtr
  * per_variable's errors and warning
  <b>Size</b>: +471 (src 354, tests 117: statistics,
  determinism); over the 400 target on its own
  <b>Verified</b>: full suite passes at df6419f.
end legend

@enduml
